meta {
  name: contact message detail
  type: http
  seq: 48
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/administrator/contact-messages/:id/
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  id: b3d91f47-2c8a-4e15-9f60-7a2d1e4c8b93
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  One enquiry. `PATCH` on the same URL marks it handled and records a note --
  see **update contact message**.

  The submitted content itself is immutable: only `handled` and `admin_notes` are
  writable, because the message is a record of what the visitor actually sent.

  ## API example response
  {
    "success": true,
    "message_detail": {
      "id": "b3d91f47-2c8a-4e15-9f60-7a2d1e4c8b93",
      "name": "Julia Brandt",
      "email": "traveller@example.com",
      "subject": "immersion",
      "subject_label": "Immersion Programme",
      "message": "Hello! I am travelling to Ecuador in November and would like to know if the Quito Immersion Program has space.",
      "programme": "",
      "handled": false,
      "handled_at": null,
      "admin_notes": "",
      "created_at": "2026-09-05T08:44:12.000000-05:00"
    }
  }
}
